{"kind":"report","text":"ready-for-review at exact clean head 4bf39626d438e71842b9c518831d9d5de2f16cad, artifact 12b68aba6824300fb21b95bea1b42fcae4e8aece.\n\nAll three blockers closed.\n\nClause admission now requires the fold's ruling. The command builds each clause source with the decision the fold recorded, and admission refuses anything the workroom did not give force to. The gap was that Projection.Statements deliberately keeps refused acts, so passing them through as if presence were force let an operator-signed clause the workroom had rejected authorize a read.\n\nAnchoring requires the charter to be cited outright rather than reached through ancestry. A rests_on edge records that an act bears on another and delegates nothing, and following the chain would have honoured clauses granted under no charter at all. This is your judgement, not mine — I flagged reachability as the more permissive reading and asked you to set it.\n\nThe composed path is tested. A command-level test runs a folded projection through clauseSources into admission and pins refused-by-the-fold, granted-under-another-charter, and no-charter-selected. Mutation-checked: passing every statement as effective admits the rejected clause. Both defects you found lived in the gap this test now covers, which is the argument for it rather than for more unit fixtures.\n\ndocs/concepts/connectors.md re-anchored from the retired inbound artifact to the current behaviour artifact, and now states the three admission conditions explicitly instead of describing them loosely enough to survive their changing.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass; the worktree is clean at this head.\n\nTwo things I want on the record rather than discovered later.\n\nThe page now rests on the artifact this head's own artifact supersedes, so it flares immediately. That is the designed cycle and the merge artifact will re-anchor it, but it means the page is stale between now and merge. While checking that I measured the whole set: ten other pages rest on retired artifacts, two of them on nothing else, so they have no live anchor at all. Recorded against request 3842d0a9 rather than fixed here.\n\nThe parent request's dogfood is still open and cannot proceed until an operator states fresh governance the right way round. That request is with hugh, corrected, and asks him to wait for this verdict.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:12b68aba6824300fb21b95bea1b42fcae4e8aece","branch":"request/github-connector-render","head":"4bf39626d438e71842b9c518831d9d5de2f16cad","status":"ready-for-review"}}